  "instructions": "Develop a paragraph from verified notes: Hana tested separate return and borrowing lines for one lunch period, recorded where delays occurred, and recommended a second trial before permanent change.",
  "parts": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "prompt": "Which assertion is most focused?",
      "response": {
        "type": "single_choice",
        "options": [
          {
            "key": "A",
            "text": "Libraries are important everywhere."
          },
          {
            "key": "B",
            "text": "A small queue trial helped Hana identify where the borrowing process slowed."
          },
          {
            "key": "C",
            "text": "Lunch can be busy."
          },
          {
            "key": "D",
            "text": "Everyone loved the new system."
          }
        ],
        "correct_key": "B",
        "choice_rationales": {
          "A": "This is too broad.",
          "B": "This states the paragraph's claim.",
          "C": "This lacks the action and insight.",
          "D": "That is unverified."
        }
      },
      "hint": "Name action and significance.",
      "correct_explanation": "The assertion establishes a testable focus."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "prompt": "Which detail best supports the method?",
      "response": {
        "type": "single_choice",
        "options": [
          {
            "key": "A",
            "text": "The library walls were blue."
          },
          {
            "key": "B",
            "text": "Hana likes mystery novels."
          },
          {
            "key": "C",
            "text": "She separated return and borrowing lines and marked when each line stopped moving."
          },
          {
            "key": "D",
            "text": "The school opened years ago."
          }
        ],
        "correct_key": "C",
        "choice_rationales": {
          "A": "This has no analytical job.",
          "B": "This is unrelated.",
          "C": "This shows the comparison method.",
          "D": "This does not support the trial."
        }
      },
      "hint": "Choose an observable procedure.",
      "correct_explanation": "The detail demonstrates how evidence was collected."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "prompt": "Which explanation develops the evidence?",
      "response": {
        "type": "single_choice",
        "options": [
          {
            "key": "A",
            "text": "The pauses showed that book scanning, not returns, caused most observed delay, so changing every counter at once would have been premature."
          },
          {
            "key": "B",
            "text": "The line was a line."
          },
          {
            "key": "C",
            "text": "The system was definitely perfect."
          },
          {
            "key": "D",
            "text": "Queues are always bad."
          }
        ],
        "correct_key": "A",
        "choice_rationales": {
          "A": "This interprets the observation cautiously.",
          "B": "This is circular.",
          "C": "The notes do not support this.",
          "D": "This overgeneralises."
        }
      },
      "hint": "Explain what the detail means.",
      "correct_explanation": "Good development connects evidence to a bounded inference."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "prompt": "Which result sentence is honest?",
      "response": {
        "type": "single_choice",
        "options": [
          {
            "key": "A",
            "text": "The trial permanently eliminated all queues."
          },
          {
            "key": "B",
            "text": "Exactly 97% of students approved."
          },
          {
            "key": "C",
            "text": "Every library should copy the design."
          },
          {
            "key": "D",
            "text": "The separate lines made the source of delay easier to see, but another trial was needed before permanent change."
          }
        ],
        "correct_key": "D",
        "choice_rationales": {
          "A": "Only one lunch period was observed.",
          "B": "No survey exists.",
          "C": "The context is too limited.",
          "D": "This matches the evidence boundary."
        }
      },
      "hint": "Respect duration and evidence.",
      "correct_explanation": "The result is useful without claiming too much."
    },
    {
